### Early life {#Early_life}

Christopher Tolkien was named after his father's friend, [Christopher Wiseman](Christopher_Wiseman.md)<sup id="cite_ref-3" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-3">[3]</a></sup> (he also sometimes used his confirmation name, "John" as seen on his initials of maps of [The Lord of the Rings](../T/The_Lord_of_the_Rings.md), "CJRT").

Born in [Leeds](../L/Leeds.md) and raised in [Oxford](../O/Oxford.md), Christopher went to the Dragon School in Oxford and Oratory School in Caversham, Berkshire. He enjoyed watching stars with a telescope as well as a passion for railways. As early as age four and five, Christopher was concerned with the consistency of *[The Hobbit](../T/The_Hobbit.md)*.

