## History {#History}

### Early history {#Early_history}

Durin's Bane was first created as a [Maia](../M/Maia.md). However, like other [evil spirits](../E/Evil_spirits.md), the Balrog followed [Morgoth](../M/Morgoth.md) to [Arda](../A/Arda.md) soon after its creation, contending with [Manwë](../M/Manwë.md) and other [Valar](../V/Valar.md).<sup id="cite_ref-2" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-2">[2]</a></sup>

It is not known in which of the [Battles of Beleriand](../B/Battles_of_Beleriand.md) Durin's Bane fought in until the end of the [First Age](../F/First_Age.md), nor whether it served under [Gothmog](<../G/Gothmog_(Lord_of_Balrogs).md>), the Lord of Balrogs. When the [Host of the Valar](../H/Host_of_the_Valar.md) defeated the hosts of Morgoth in the [War of Wrath](../W/War_of_Wrath.md), Durin's Bane managed to flee the overthrow of [Thangorodrim](../T/Thangorodrim.md) and escaped into the east and hid in the roots of the [Misty Mountains](../M/Misty_Mountains.md) beneath [Khazad-dûm](../M/Moria.md).<sup id="cite_ref-Durin_3-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Durin-3">[3]</a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-4" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-4">[4]</a></sup>

### Awakening and the Third Age {#Awakening_and_the_Third_Age}

