## Other versions of the legendarium {#Other_versions_of_the_legendarium}

In the *[The Grey Annals](../T/The_Grey_Annals.md)*, created in the 1930s,<sup id="cite_ref-4" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-4">[4]</a></sup> Bëor was directly followed by Bregolas and [Barahir](Barahir.md), who were his sons (and Bregolas was born in [F.A.](../F/First_Age.md) [400](../F/First_Age_400.md)<sup id="cite_ref-5" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-5">[5]</a></sup>). After publication of *[The Lord of the Rings](../T/The_Lord_of_the_Rings.md)* a new genealogy for the [House of Bëor](../H/House_of_Bëor.md) was made in the 1950s and at that time four generations were inserted after Bëor, with Bregor becoming the father of Bregolas and Barahir.<sup id="cite_ref-6" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-6">[6]</a></sup>

