## Other versions of the legendarium {#Other_versions_of_the_legendarium}

A late draft of what would later become the chapter "[Many Meetings](../M/Many_Meetings.md)" mentions that the realm of Brand "included Esgaroth, and much land to the south of the great falls".<sup id="cite_ref-31" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-31">[31]</a></sup>

In two plot notes for *[The Hobbit](../T/The_Hobbit.md)*, Girion is referred to as "king of Dale".<sup id="cite_ref-32" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-32">[32]</a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-33" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-33">[33]</a></sup> In earlier versions of what would later become the chapters "[Inside Information](../I/Inside_Information.md)" and "[Fire and Water](../F/Fire_and_Water.md)", Girion is already referred to as "lord of Dale".<sup id="cite_ref-34" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-34">[34]</a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-35" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-35">[35]</a></sup>

