## History {#History}

By the time Argeleb came to power, the line of kings had failed in the kingdoms of [Cardolan](../C/Cardolan.md) and [Rhudaur](../R/Rhudaur.md), so Argeleb claimed sovereignty over all of [Arnor](Arnor.md)<sup id="cite_ref-Eriador_3-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Eriador-3">[3]</a></sup> (taking the royal prefix *[ar(a)-](Ar.md)* as a token of this<sup id="cite_ref-4" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-4">[4]</a></sup>). He was thus not only the seventh King of [Arthedain](Arthedain.md), but also the seventeenth King of [Arnor](Arnor.md). Cardolan accepted this rule but Rhudaur resisted this claim, and a captain of the [Hill-men](../H/Hill-men.md) of that land formed a secret alliance with Arnor's enemy, the [Witch-king](../W/Witch-king.md) of [Angmar](Angmar.md). In response, Argeleb fortified the [hills](../W/Weather_Hills.md), but he was killed during battle with the two realms in [T.A.](../T/Third_Age.md) [1356](../T/Third_Age_1356.md).<sup id="cite_ref-Eriador_3-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Eriador-3">[3]</a></sup><sup id="cite_ref-5" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-5">[5]</a></sup>

Argeleb ruled for only seven years, and was succeeded by his son, [Arveleg I](Arveleg_I.md), upon his death in [T.A.](../T/Third_Age.md) [1356](../T/Third_Age_1356.md).<sup id="cite_ref-North_2-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-North-2">[2]</a></sup>

