## Other versions of the legendarium {#Other_versions_of_the_legendarium}

[Elentir](../E/Elentir.md), intended to be a brother of Amandil, was a character developed but never fully adapted into the formal history of Númenor. In one version of the story of [Ar-Pharazôn](Ar-Pharazôn.md), his future wife [Míriel](../T/Tar-Míriel.md), the daughter of the current king, was betrothed to Elentir. However, she fell desperately in love with Pharazôn and chose to become his queen when he took up the [Sceptre of Númenor](../S/Sceptre_of_Númenor.md). This story is very different than the tale in the published *[The Silmarillion](../T/The_Silmarillion.md)*, where Ar-Pharazôn takes Míriel very much against her will in order to claim the Sceptre. In either case, Elentir disappeared before Nùmendil died, leaving Amandil as the [Lord of Andúnië](../L/Lords_of_Andúnië.md).<sup id="cite_ref-AkallabethPM_5-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-AkallabethPM-5">[5]</a></sup>

