## The Battle {#The_Battle}

The North Army led by the [Ruling Steward](../R/Ruling_Steward.md) [Cirion](../C/Cirion.md) counter-attacked, and was driven into the *Wold*, cut off from the later reinforcements by the Balchoth host. By the time the [Southern Army](../S/Southern_Army.md) appeared, the North Army had come under attack by an [Orc](../O/Orcs.md) band [from the Misty Mountains](../O/Orcs_of_the_Misty_Mountains.md) which by chance or design had descended from the mountains, and the [Dúnedain](../D/Dúnedain.md) were backed against the river in a hopeless situation.

At this time the Éothéod under their leader [Eorl the Young](../E/Eorl.md) suddenly appeared, unexpected by friend or foe, as they were belatedly responding to a previous request by Cirion. The Éothéod crossed the Anduin at the *Undeeps* of the river, and broke on the rearguard of the Balchoth. The Balchoth were completely defeated and the Gondorian armies saved. The Éothéod continued their foray into northern Gondor, scattering and destroying all the Balchoth in Calenardhon.

